# Copy to .env.local and set as MANY of the keys below as you like.
#
# Every key you set joins a failover chain, in the order listed. When one
# provider's free tier runs out for the minute, the request moves to the next
# one automatically — so with three or four free keys the app effectively
# never stops. AI_PROVIDER moves one provider to the front of the chain.
#
# AI_PROVIDER=groq

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recommended. Free, no card.
# https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# The default model (openai/gpt-oss-120b) is capable but has NO web access on
# its own. Switch to a compound model to turn on model-native web search:
#   GROQ_MODEL=groq/compound
# Model IDs get retired — llama-3.3-70b-versatile went on 2026-08-16. Check
# https://console.groq.com/docs/models for what is current.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other free options. None of these can search the web on their own, but with
# TAVILY_API_KEY set (below) every one of them answers from sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Free, no card, and serves DeepSeek — the free way to get DeepSeek.
# https://cloud.sambanova.ai/apis
# SAMBANOVA_API_KEY=
# SAMBANOVA_MODEL=DeepSeek-V3.2

# Free with an NVIDIA developer account. Also serves DeepSeek (V4).
# https://build.nvidia.com
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_MODEL=deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813

# If a provider retires a model ID, the app asks it for the current list,
# picks the best fit automatically, and tells you what it chose. Set the
# *_MODEL variable only when you want to pin a specific one.

# https://cloud.cerebras.ai
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b

# https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-large-latest

# https://openrouter.ai/keys — free only on ":free" models.
# A ":online" suffix adds web search but is billed per result.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# https://github.com/settings/tokens — needs the models:read scope
# GITHUB_MODELS_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_MODELS_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paid — placed last in the chain so they are only used once every free tier
# above is exhausted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Searches and cites by default. Pro subscribers get a monthly API credit.
# https://www.perplexity.ai/settings/api
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=
# PERPLEXITY_MODEL=sonar-pro

# DeepSeek direct: very cheap but needs a top-up; there is no free tier.
# For free DeepSeek use SambaNova above, or an OpenRouter ":free" model.
# https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# ===========================================================================
# WEB SEARCH — independent of the model provider.
# With one of these set, ANY model above gets grounded, cited answers: the
# app runs the searches and hands the results to the model. Both free.
# ===========================================================================

# Recommended. 1,000 searches/month free, no card.
# https://app.tavily.com
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Alternative. 2,000 searches/month free.
# https://api.search.brave.com
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# TOKEN BUDGET (optional)
# Per-request input budget. Each provider has a default tuned to its free
# tier's per-minute cap; raise it on a paid tier. Long documents are read
# in parts that fit this budget.
# ===========================================================================
# AI_BUDGET_TOKENS=9000
